<style>
  /* Cookie table styles — not in base.css */
  .cookie-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.75rem; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 12px; }
  .cookie-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; min-width: 580px; }
  .cookie-table thead th { background: var(--deep); color: #fff; text-align: left; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.9rem 1rem; }
  .cookie-table tbody td { padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.06); vertical-align: top; color: #3a3a3a; }
  .cookie-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--cream); }
  .cookie-table td code { font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--deep); background: rgba(225,0,114,0.07); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; }
</style>

<!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
<section id="main" tabindex="-1" style="position:relative;padding:6rem 2rem 4.5rem;background:linear-gradient(155deg,var(--deep) 0%,#6d0339 60%,var(--pink) 100%);color:#fff;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;">
  <div style="position:absolute;top:-100px;right:-100px;width:340px;height:340px;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle,var(--yellow) 0%,var(--orange) 60%,transparent 75%);opacity:0.25;filter:blur(8px);pointer-events:none;"></div>
  <div style="position:relative;max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--yellow);margin-bottom:1.2rem;">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,4.6rem);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Cookie<br>Policy.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);max-width:540px;margin:0 auto;">Last updated: May 2026. The small (but tasty) print.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ COOKIE CONTENT ══ -->
<section style="padding:5rem 2rem 6rem;background:#fff;">
  <div class="legal-doc">

    <div class="legal-toc">
      <p>Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#what">What cookies are</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how">How we use cookies</a></li>
        <li><a href="#categories">Cookie categories</a></li>
        <li><a href="#table">Cookies we use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#manage">Managing your preferences</a></li>
        <li><a href="#browser">Browser controls</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <h2 id="what">1. What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files that a website saves to your device (your computer, phone or tablet) when you visit. They're widely used to make sites work — or work more efficiently — and to give site owners information about how the site is being used.</p>
    <p>"Similar technologies" includes things like web beacons, pixels, local storage and tags. For simplicity we refer to all of these as "cookies" in this policy.</p>

    <h2 id="how">2. How we use cookies</h2>
    <p>We use cookies for a few specific reasons:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>To make the site work — for example, remembering that you've passed the age gate, or holding the contents of your basket while you shop.</li>
      <li>To remember your preferences and make your experience smoother on return visits.</li>
      <li>To understand how the site is performing and how visitors use it, so we can improve things.</li>
      <li>With your consent, to show you relevant marketing on other sites you visit and to measure how well our campaigns are doing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We only set non-essential cookies if you've given us consent via our cookie banner.</p>

    <h2 id="categories">3. Cookie categories</h2>
    <p>We group cookies into four categories, in line with ICO guidance:</p>

    <h3>Strictly necessary</h3>
    <p>These cookies are essential for the site to function. They include things like remembering that you've confirmed your age, keeping you signed in, holding items in your basket and protecting against cross-site request forgery (CSRF). You can't switch these off because the site won't work properly without them.</p>

    <h3>Functional</h3>
    <p>These cookies remember choices you make to give you a better experience — for example, recently viewed products, your preferred delivery region or whether you've dismissed a notification. Turning them off won't break the site, but some features may behave less helpfully.</p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>These cookies — set by Google Analytics 4 and Shopify Analytics — help us understand how visitors find and use the site, which pages are popular and where things can be improved. The data is aggregated and we don't use it to identify you personally.</p>

    <h3>Marketing</h3>
    <p>These cookies — set by Google Ads, Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel, TikTok Pixel and Pinterest Tag — let us show you relevant Sencillo ads on other websites and social platforms, and measure how those ads perform. They are only set if you've given us consent.</p>

    <h2 id="table">4. Cookies we use</h2>
    <p>Here's the current list of cookies set on sencillodrinks.com. We'll update this as our tooling changes.</p>

    <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
      <table class="cookie-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Type</th><th>Expiry</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>sencilloAgeVerified</code></td>
            <td>Remembers that you've confirmed you're 18 or over so we don't show the age gate on every page.</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary</td>
            <td>Session</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>sencilloCookieConsent</code></td>
